        "label": "Heat Pump Feedforward",
        "disabled": false,
        "info": "Feedforward water temperature from the outside temperature",
        "env": []
    },
    {
        "type": "comment",
        "name": "Heat Pump Feedforward (readme)",
        "info": "# Heat pump feedforward\n\nCalculates the feedforward water temperature from the current outside temperature:\n`water_temp = slope * outside_temp + intercept`, limited to the min / max water temperature.\n\n## Heating curve\nSelect with `input_select.heat_pump_feedforward_source`:\n- **Manual**: `input_number.heat_pump_feedforward_manual_slope` / `_manual_intercept`\n- **History**: the curve calculated by the `Heat Pump History` flow. Falls back to Manual\n  as long as the history has not been calculated.\n\n## Simple day schedule (mild weather)\nBelow 24 °C water temperature the curve is replaced by a simple schedule, effective when\nthe 24h average outside temperature >= `input_number.heat_pump_feedforward_simple_outside_temperature`:\n- heat at 24 °C from `input_datetime.heat_pump_feedforward_simple_start_time` (default midnight)\n- stop for the rest of the day once `sensor.heat_pump_inside_temperature`\n  >= `input_number.heat_pump_feedforward_simple_stop_inside_temperature`\n- `heating` is false while stopped: switch the heat pump off\n\n## Output\n- `global.heat_pump_feedforward` for use in other flows\n- Home Assistant event `heat_pump_feedforward` -> `sensor.heat_pump_feedforward_water_temperature`\n  and `binary_sensor.heat_pump_feedforward_heating`",
        "x": 160,
        "y": 40,
        "wires": [],
        "id": "1e7d9319fd2199d8",
        "z": "30c1cadb3f5445db"
    },
